# Architecture summary

This design separates the Sales Intelligence platform into **two primary user journeys**:

1. **Conversational AI path** — stateful, streaming, agent-based interactions.
2. **Insights and reporting path** — deterministic KPI retrieval, dashboards, reports, and LLM-generated explanations.

Both paths share the same identity, API security, LLM gateway, enterprise data, observability, and deployment capabilities.

A strong message for the meeting is:

> **Databricks, Snowflake, and PostgreSQL calculate and serve the facts. The LLM explains the facts and orchestrates actions; it is not the system of record.**

---

# Architecture planes

The diagram is organized into architectural planes.

| Plane                        | Purpose                                                             |
| ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| User Experience              | Everything the user sees and interacts with                         |
| Security and Access          | Authentication, authorization, API protection, and compliance       |
| Runtime Plane                | Executes chat, agents, reporting, and insight-generation requests   |
| LLM Control Plane            | Centralizes prompts, safety, model access, and provider abstraction |
| Data Plane                   | Stores operational, serving, and historical analytical data         |
| Observability and Governance | Monitors performance, quality, security, and cost                   |
| Platform Plane               | Builds, deploys, and provisions the platform                        |

