# Zone 6 — Observability and Governance

## LLM observability

LLM observability measures how AI requests behave.

It should track:

* Prompt version
* Model and endpoint
* Token usage
* Cost
* End-to-end latency
* Time to first token
* Tool calls
* Agent steps
* Retrieval results
* Guardrail decisions
* User feedback
* Response quality
* Error rate
* Hallucination or groundedness evaluation

A complete trace might look like:

```text
APIM request
→ Conversation runtime
→ Agent plan
→ SQL tool
→ Context builder
→ LLM call
→ Output guardrail
→ Web PubSub response
```

All steps should share the same correlation ID.

---

## Infrastructure metrics

Infrastructure metrics monitor the technical health of the system.

Important metrics include:

* API response time
* HTTP error rate
* PostgreSQL connection usage
* Query latency
* Service Bus queue depth
* Dead-letter message count
* Web PubSub connection count
* Worker CPU and memory
* LLM endpoint failures
* Databricks job duration
* Daily KPI refresh status
* Data freshness
* Uptime

Service-level objectives should be defined separately for chat and reporting.

For example:

```text
Reporting API: 95% under 2 seconds
Chat first token: 95% under 3 seconds
Daily KPI snapshot: available by 6:00 AM
```

---

## Security and audit

This is the centralized governance view across the complete platform.

It should consolidate:

* Identity logs
* Authorization decisions
* API activity
* Data-access logs
* Prompt and model changes
* Tool execution
* Admin operations
* Security alerts
* Vulnerability findings
* Compliance reports

The Audit and Compliance box in Zone 2 focuses on enforcement at API access. Zone 6 provides centralized monitoring and reporting across the entire platform.

