# Five-minute meeting talk track

> This architecture supports two distinct sales intelligence experiences: conversational AI and insights/reporting. Users access both through a React application and authenticate through Entra ID. All APIs are protected by Azure API Management, RBAC, rate limiting, and audit controls.
>
> The conversational path uses Web PubSub for real-time response streaming, Service Bus for durable asynchronous work, and an agent orchestrator containing planner and executor capabilities. Agents access enterprise systems only through approved tools and connectors.
>
> The reporting path uses precomputed KPIs and aggregations. Databricks calculates these metrics daily from Snowflake data. The authoritative analytical snapshot is retained in the Snowflake/Iceberg layer, while a minimal serving copy is moved into PostgreSQL to provide predictable application latency.
>
> All AI requests pass through a centralized LLM Gateway. The gateway manages prompts, constructs context, applies input and output guardrails, masks sensitive information, and routes requests to approved model endpoints such as Claude.
>
> Finally, the platform includes end-to-end observability, security auditing, CI/CD, and Terraform-based infrastructure deployment. The core principle is that databases and deterministic processing produce the facts, while the LLM explains those facts and helps orchestrate authorized actions.

The most important line to emphasize is:

> **We are not replacing governed analytics with an LLM. We are placing a governed AI experience on top of deterministic, authorized, and precomputed enterprise data.**
